# Docker build context for images built from the repository root (the worker on Fly, D-13).
# Images never contain environment files: hosted environments take configuration only from the
# platform's environment variables (docs/14-ENVIRONMENTS-DEPLOY.md section 2).
# scripts/checks/env-files.sh exports the build context and fails if any env file is in it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.envrc
!**/.env.example

# Keypairs and local chain state (the same patterns as .gitignore)
**/*keypair*.json
**/wallet-*.json
**/id.json
**/*-deployer.json
**/*.keypair
.cache
.localnet
test-ledger

# Dependencies and build outputs: images install and build their own
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/out
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
target

# The demo video's project (step 4.5): no image needs it, and its cut media is large
video

# Repository metadata
.git
**/.DS_Store
